    "title": "Fri 11/13 · October PPI after the Nvidia shock",
    "body": "October PPI rose **0.3%** m/m, cooler than the 0.4% expected, after a 1.4% jump in September (revised from 1.3%); it is up 6.5% from a year ago, the most since November 2022. Core (ex food and energy) rose 0.3% as expected. Futures firmed after the print, with the 10-year near **5.13%**. A December hike was priced at about 89% before the data, and Bowman speaks at 10:50a. Nvidia, now run by interim CEO Colette Kress, reports Tue 11/17 after the close."
