  "stories": [
    {
      "title": "Jensen Huang resigns at Nvidia.",
      "body": "Nvidia said at 8:48a Thursday that Jensen Huang resigned as president, CEO and director, effective immediately, after reports of extramarital affairs. CFO Colette Kress is interim CEO and former Synopsys CEO Harvey Jones becomes board chair. NVDA fell as much as 14% at the open, then closed −4.3% at $166.19; it is down 11% this week and more than 30% below its Oct 6 peak. Money rotated to rivals: AMD +5.9%, Broadcom +5.5%, Arista +5.1%. Super Micro fell 11% on reports of Justice Department inquiries. NVDA was up about 2% pre-market Friday. Earnings stay on Tue 11/17. Polymarket gives about 25% that a permanent CEO is named by Dec 31.",
