      "body": "The 10-year rose about 10bp to roughly 5.10% Thursday and the 2-year about 12bp to 4.87%, after a soft 30-year auction and hawkish Fed talk: Hammack wants policy in restrictive territory and Daly and Goolsbee see more tightening likely. Tuesday's October CPI rose 0.4% (core 0.3%, a third straight 0.3%). Jobless claims rose to 200K (195K expected). Prediction markets price a 25bp hike on Dec 9 at about 85% and 50bp at about 10%. Friday's October PPI came in cooler at +0.3% (0.4% expected, core 0.3% as expected), though it is up 6.5% from a year ago; the 10-year eased to about 5.13% after the print.",
