    {
      "title": "Cisco and Applied Materials beat; Cerebras misses.",
      "body": "Cisco posted record fiscal Q1 revenue of $18.5B (+24%) and non-GAAP EPS of $1.40, raised its full-year revenue outlook to $74.8–75.8B and now expects about $9B of AI infrastructure revenue from hyperscalers, more than double its prior view; shares rose after hours. Applied Materials earned $4.16 a share on revenue of $10.41B (about $10.3B expected) and guided Q1 to about $11.1B and $4.35, above estimates; shares, −3.6% in the session, edged up after hours. Cerebras grew revenue 55% to $210.8M, short of about $214.7M expected, with a GAAP loss of $0.67 a share, but raised its full-year outlook and reported $26.1B of remaining performance obligations. Cerebras jumped about 16% pre-market Friday."
    },
    {
      "title": "Oil jumps as Trump says no Iran deal needed.",
      "body": "Trump said the US does not need a deal with Iran, casting doubt on reported talks. WTI settled up $2.21 (+2.6%) at $88.74 and Brent up $3.06 (+3.3%) at $95.82, despite EIA builds in crude and fuel stocks. Energy (+1.5%) was the best S&P sector, while airlines slid on fuel costs: United −6.0%, Delta −5.2%. Higher oil is the wrong direction for the inflation picture going into PPI."
    },
